14.04.2006, 16:45 Arnt Richard Johansen wrote:

> On Fri, 14 Apr 2006, Yanis Batura wrote:

>> Can {pe do} be negated, like in English
>> "I like all cars that are not of you.", or
>> "I like all [not-your] cars."

> Not that I know of, but any sumti can be negated with {na'e bo}.

> Thus:
> mi nelci ro lo karce pe na'e bo do

I dare to rejoin that the meaning of "all cars that pertain to not-
you" is somewhat different from "all cars that not- pertain to you".

